# Git workflow

Work only on `main`. Never create a branch, local or remote.

When the user accepts a change, commit it on `main` and push to `origin/main`. That push is the production release: GitHub Actions builds the site and publishes it to the `gh-pages` branch, which serves micalingo.com.

Do not push, reset, or delete `gh-pages`. It is the published site, not a working branch. Its behind/ahead counts versus `main` are normal, because it stores built files, not source history.

Delete leftover feature branches only when their commits are already in `main`.
